{%- comment -%}
  Organization chart section
  Place in /sections/org-chart.liquid

  Uses the CPU CBA theme tokens and classes (section, page-width, section-head,
  eyebrow, lede, etc.). Pure Liquid + CSS, no JavaScript needed.

  HOW TO EDIT THE CHART
  In the section settings, paste one person per line, in top-to-bottom order:

    level | name | position | credentials | options | width

  - level       : 0 = top (Dean), 1 = reports to the Dean, 2 = reports to a level 1 person, and so on
  - name        : the person's name
  - position    : job title (can be blank)
  - credentials : degrees. Separate several with a semicolon (;)
  - options     : blank, or one of
                    staff  = lighter card for secretaries / support staff
                    group  = a label (e.g. Faculty) whose people below it are shown as a grid
                    aside  = card shown beside the person above it (used for the Dean's secretary)
  - width       : (optional, level 1 only) column width. 1 = normal, 2 = twice as wide

  If the box is left blank, the built-in CBA chart below is shown.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign bg = section.settings.background
  assign section_class = 'section'
  if bg == 'cream'
    assign section_class = 'section section--cream'
  elsif bg == 'paper'
    assign section_class = 'section section--paper'
  elsif bg == 'navy'
    assign section_class = 'section section--navy on-dark'
  endif
-%}

